    (aidendle94/sparkrun-sglang-inkling2-gb10, from experimental-1.1) carries one such module, built by this script
    from its own base image, at /opt/inkling2-spark/prebuilt/; the image also carries this NOTICE and the licence
    texts it names, under /opt/inkling2-spark.
    FlashInfer's distribution carries a NOTICE file. Its attribution notices, which apply to the excerpts above:
    "FlashInfer / Copyright 2025-2026 NVIDIA / Copyright 2023-2026 FlashInfer community (https://flashinfer.ai/)".
    The other entries of that file name components (the KDA kernels and others) of which this recipe carries nothing.

Trained for this recipe: patches/gate-head-mlp-reg.pt, a 256-unit confidence head for the speculative-decoding gate
(docs/results.md). It was fit by the author on hidden states and step distributions that the draft bundled with
thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small produced on the author's fleet for a generated load (bench/conf_capture_run.py; no
request of another client was recorded). The file holds the head's own parameters, with a projection fitted on
those hidden states folded in; it holds no weight of the model.

bench/exp_combo.py carries no licence line of its own: the head file records the sha256 of the script that trained
it, so its bytes are left as they were. It is under the same MIT terms as the rest of this recipe.

Method references (no code taken): block verification follows Sun et al., "Block Verification Accelerates
Speculative Decoding", arXiv 2403.10444 (bench/bv_exact.py checks it under this recipe's gate). The packed block
scales (patches/scale_pack.py) take the idea of keeping compressed scale factors resident from the compressed scale
layout of NVIDIA's hyperflare-inference (github.com/NVIDIA/hyperflare-inference, Apache License 2.0); the format, the
Triton expansion kernel, the decode routine and the code are this recipe's, and the forked GEMM is the derived work
described above.

